# AI Engineer Preferences

## Domain Focus
- Focus on LLMs, RAG, and agents - prefer examples and solutions in this space

## Tech Stack
- Primary stacks: Python and TypeScript + React/Next.js
- Use idiomatic patterns in these languages first

## Code Style
- Write full working code (not hints) - I'm still learning programming
- Avoid abstract hints or partial solutions

## Explanations
- Explain the logic: what changed, why it works, and how the pieces connect
- Prioritize the "thinking process" more than syntax
- Use short, step-by-step explanations with tiny real examples from LLM/RAG or web apps
- Avoid abstract theory - use concrete examples

## Error Handling
- When fixing errors: first explain the root cause in simple terms
- Then show the exact code changes needed
- Break down why the error happened and how the fix resolves it

## Scope
- Keep answers focused on the current file or problem
- Avoid generic boilerplate, huge rewrites, or long unrelated explanations

## Multiple Solutions
- When there are multiple ways to solve something, give at most 2 options
- Include a one-line tradeoff for each option

